    "secondary_details_M3cr8M": {
      "type": "secondary-details",
      "disabled": true,
      "name": "Secondary Details",
      "settings": {
        "style": "bg-white",
        "heading": "Removes >95% of Fluoride  with “First-of-its-Kind” Filtration System",
        "content": "<p>Fluoride is added to public drinking water for approximately three out of four Americans. However, <a href=\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3876610/\" title=\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3876610/\">there is growing concern in the scientific community that excessive fluoride levels could potentially be toxic to the brain or even increase the risk of the rare cancer, osteosarcoma.<br/></a><br/>Designed as an essential add-on to our Gravity Water Filter system, our scientists have developed athe first refillable stainless steel fluoride filter designed for home gravity systems.that removes more than 95% of fluoride from drinking water while retaining essential nutrients. Arsenic<br/><br/>Engineered for everyday use, the filter requires a simple top-up of the proprietary filtration media every four months or after treating up to 1,060 gallons of water. This makes it the most effective and sustainable fluoride removal system on the market, helping you maintain a healthy lifestyle.<br/></p>",
        "buttonlink": "",
        "buttontext": "",
        "afterbutton": "",
        "custom_id": ""
      }
    },
    "copy_image_DfRFKh": {
      "type": "copy-image",
      "settings": {
        "style": "bg-light",
        "layout": "image-copy",
        "vertical_align": "align-items-center",
        "heading": "WARNING: Drinking tap water makes 7.2 million americans sick every year!",
        "content": "<p>Every year, millions of Americans fall ill from ingesting harmful chemicals in tap water. In Baltimore, a parasite was recently detected in the drinking water; in California’s Coachella Valley, water from fast-food soda fountains tested positive for salmonella; and in Iowa, unsafe levels of nitrate and alachlor were found.<br/><br/>These contaminants have been linked to a range of serious health issues, including liver and kidney damage, thyroid disease, cancer, and even “blue baby syndrome” in infants.<br/><br/>Phoenix Gravity Water Filters use advanced Nano adsorption filtration technology to remove 99.9% of contaminants from tap water, making it safe to drink no matter where you live in the U.S.</p>",
