    "accordion_tabs_kBhDkz": {
      "type": "accordion-tabs",
      "blocks": {
        "tab_HPXac4": {
          "type": "tab",
          "settings": {
            "tab_title": "Set Up & Maintenance"
          }
        },
        "question_answer_K38zCJ": {
          "type": "question_answer",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is It Essential To Prime The Carbon Filter Elements?",
            "answer": "<p>Priming the Carbon Filter Elements is the first step to ensuring your filters are completely free of any residuals from the manufacturing process. The residuals are completely normal and safe but can lead to cloudy water if the filters are not correctly primed.</p><p>We recommend priming your Carbon Filter Elements for at least three minutes. If not primed sufficiently, the first four rounds of filtered water may have cloudy white particles that can be safely discarded.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_answer_YH9Tyg": {
          "type": "question_answer",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "question": "Why Is My Water Cloudy?",
            "answer": "<p>Don’t worry, cloudy water after initial installation is normal and completely harmless. It’s simply safe residual dust from the manufacturing process. It can occur if the filters are not correctly primed - and we recommend priming filters fully (see above).</p><p>If it is not primed, it can take about four rounds of filtered water to clear.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_answer_jEVb8T": {
          "type": "question_answer",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How Long Will the POSTreat™ Fluoride Removal Filter Elements Last?",
            "answer": "<p>The POSTreat™ Fluoride Removal Filter Elements are precision crafted from premium AISI 304 stainless steel. Built to perform for up to 10 years, it is backed by our 10 Year Warranty.Inside each element is our proprietary FluoRid media, specially formulated for highly effective fluoride reduction. The media is rated for up to 1,060 gallons of filtration capacity and typically requires replacement approximately every 4 months, depending on water quality and usage.We also offer a refill media subscription service. We’ll keep track of your replacement schedule and send your refill media when it’s time, so you can enjoy uninterrupted performance without the hassle.<br/><br/></p>"
          }
        },
        "question_answer_iD9QdM": {
          "type": "question_answer",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How Long Will The POSTreat Fluoride Removal Filter Elements Last?",
            "answer": "<p>Our POSTreat Fluoride Removal Filter Elements are made from ASI 304-Stainless Steel and are designed to last for years - which is why we included a 1 year warranty with our products.</p><p>The proprietary FluoRid media will last for 1060 gallons and need replacing approximately 4 months. </p><p>We also offer a subscription service for replacement media - we’ll remember when they’re due, so you don’t have to. </p>"
          }
        },
        "question_answer_jQNRA4": {
          "type": "question_answer",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How Frequently Do I Need To Change My Filter Elements?",
            "answer": "<p>This depends on the usage frequency and quality of your water input. We recommend replacing them at the following milestones:Carbon Filter Elements: 12 months.POSTreat FluoRid Refill Media: 4 months</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_answer_nfPQrG": {
          "type": "question_answer",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Will I Be Able To Assemble My System And Change My Filters Myself?",
            "answer": "<p>Certainly! Our systems are designed to be extremely easy to assemble and everything you need will be included. You can do it yourself with just your hands - there’s no specialist tools, plumbers or electricians required.</p><p>We include full instructions with every unit and we’re always here to help. </p>"
          }
        },
        "question_answer_X8BdNU": {
          "type": "question_answer",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "question": "My Phoenix Gravity Water Filter Has Water Dripping In Between The Upper And Lower Chambers, What Does This Mean?",
            "answer": "<p>This will be from over-filling the Water Filter System. Careful use can help prevent overfilling by checking how much water is in the lower chamber before filling the upper chamber.</p><p>Once you get to know your usage rates the re-filling process will become second nature!</p><p>We also sell a Stainless Steel Spigot With Water Level Gauge which will enable you to see the water level from the outside.  </p>"
          }
        },
        "question_answer_UDnhbf": {
          "type": "question_answer",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How Frequently Do I Need To Change My Filter Elements?",
            "answer": "<p>This depends on the usage frequency and quality of your water input. As a guide, we recommend replacing them at the following milestones:</p><p>Carbon Filter Elements: 12 months.</p><p>POSTreat (and FluoRid Media Refill): 4 months</p><p>We also offer a subscription service, which also works out to 5% off each order. Let us remind you when you need to change your filters, so you don’t have to!</p>"
          }
        },
        "tab_WjcFUA": {
          "type": "tab",
          "settings": {
            "tab_title": "Filtration"
          }
        },
        "question_answer_yUixgf": {
          "type": "question_answer",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "question": "What Do Your Filters Really Remove?",
            "answer": "<p>Phoenix Gravity POSTreat™ Filter Elements are precision engineered using premium AISI 304 stainless steel housings and prefilled proprietary FluoRid media for advanced fluoride reduction performance. These high efficiency filter elements are designed to remove more than 95% of fluoride from drinking water while maintaining clean, great tasting water.Unlike many conventional filtration solutions, Phoenix Gravity POSTreat™ Filter Elements do not leach harmful chemicals, additives, or unwanted by-products back into your water, delivering a safer, cleaner, and more reliable filtration experience with every use.<br/><br/></p>"
          }
        },
        "question_answer_TwmjtY": {
          "type": "question_answer",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What Do Your Filters Really Remove?",
            "answer": "<p>Phoenix Gravity Carbon Filter Elements are made from pure coconut shells, which are a sustainable and renewable resource. The carbon in the filters is activated, which means that it has a high surface area and is very porous. This allows it to trap a wide range of contaminants, including chlorine, heavy metals, and other impurities. </p><p>Phoenix Gravity Carbon Filters removes microplastics down to 5 microns in size and also eliminates PFAs, Hormones and Pharmaceutical residues from the water. Phoenix Gravity Carbon Filters are designed to provide clean, odorless water with a great taste. They do not release any harmful chemicals or by-products into the water, and they are very effective at removing chlorine and other volatile organic compounds.  A pair of carbon filter elements can filter gallons of water by providing safe and healthy drinking water.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_answer_9yMg4X": {
          "type": "question_answer",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do Phoenix Gravity Filters Remove Residual Pharmaceutical Waste?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes, up to 99.99%! our primary Carbon Filter Elements have been independently tested for many Volatile Organic compounds including 1,4- dichlorobenzene, 2-Butanone, Acetone, Allyl Chloride and many more.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_answer_YaqX9K": {
          "type": "question_answer",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do Your Filters Remove Fluoride?",
            "answer": "<p>They certainly can! We’ve designed a specialist fluoride removal filter called the POSTreat to remove over 95% of fluoride from your tap water.</p><p>Made from the ASI 304 Grade Stainless Steel, it’s completely reusable and refillable, with our POSTreat FluoRid Media Refill. The POSTtreat can be used in conjunction with primary Carbon Filter Elements.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_answer_8w4QRz": {
          "type": "question_answer",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do Phoenix Carbon Elements Eliminate Phthalates From Water?",
            "answer": "<p>While we have not specifically tested for the removal of phthalates, our Phoenix Carbon Filter Elements are made with highest grade activated coconut carbon, which is known for its effectiveness in adsorbing phthalates from water. We are constantly improving and testing our filters.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_answer_TYE6gG": {
          "type": "question_answer",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do Phoenix Gravity Filters Remove Estrogen?",
            "answer": "<p>While we have not specifically tested for the removal of estrogen, our Phoenix Carbon Filter Elements are made with activated coconut carbon, which is known for its effectiveness in adsorbing estrogen from water. We are constantly improving and testing our filters.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_answer_6C7C4q": {
          "type": "question_answer",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How Do Your Gravity Filters And Filter Elements Compare To Others?",
            "answer": "<p>We are one of the leaders in advanced Gravity Filtration. With over 50 plus years’ experience of manufacturing in-house, we have complete control over the process and the quality of our filters and filter elements. We are enormously proud of the effort it has taken us to become a leading manufacturer of Gravity Water Filters.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_answer_rzDw8m": {
          "type": "question_answer",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Are Your Filters As Comprehensive As Berkey?",
            "answer": "<p>Absolutely! We have run extensive and independent tests on our filters for a variety of chemical contaminants such as Lead, chlorine, chromium, Volatile organic compounds and 100 more.</p><p>What’s more, with over 50 plus years’ experience of in-house manufacturing - we’re one of the leading global manufacturers of  AISI 304 Grade Stainless Steel gravity filtration systems. We also have complete control over the process and the quality of our filters and replacement filter elements. We are enormously proud of the effort it has taken us to become the world’s leading manufacturer of Gravity Water Filters.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_answer_XdWRAV": {
          "type": "question_answer",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do Phoenix Gravity Filters Lower The TDS?",
            "answer": "<p>TDS stands for Total Dissolved Solids and is measured in parts per million (ppm) or parts per billion (ppb). It’s a measure of the water’s organic and inorganic content including minerals and nutrients.</p><p>Natural water will have a TDS reading from minerals and nutrients picked up from the rocks and ground it flows through. It’s generally accepted that 300 ppm is a good mineral content. We purposely do not bring our TDS to zero, because we’re all about preserving the natural vitamins and minerals your body needs.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_answer_6UmfCk": {
          "type": "question_answer",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "question": "What Is Inside The Filter Element Box?",
            "answer": "<p>Phoenix Gravity Carbon Filter Elements includes the following accessories, 1) Filter elements pre-fitted with wingnut and washers 2) ASI 304 Grade Stainless steel spigot  3) Lid Knob 4) A single spare set of Washers and wingnut in case the existing filter washer and wing nut are damaged or misplaced 5) A spare hole blockers 6) instruction manual</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_answer_N8dCix": {
          "type": "question_answer",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "question": "Will Phoenix Gravity Filters Remove Water Hardness?",
            "answer": "<p>No. Phoenix Carbon Filter Elements are designed to remove up to 99.99% of chlorine, lead and over 100 other unwanted substances from your drinking water.</p>"
          }
        },
        "tab_iwXnJF": {
          "type": "tab",
          "settings": {
            "tab_title": "Shipping & Returns"
          }
        },
        "question_answer_9yN6Fe": {
          "type": "question_answer",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do I need the stainless steel casing for the POSTreat Fluoride Removal Filters?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes, the stainless steel casing is essential. It holds the media inside. This optimized interaction with water enhances fluoride reduction and overall effectiveness. The AISI 304 stainless steel is reusable and refillable with the FluoRid media once in 4 months.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_answer_mFXChh": {
          "type": "question_answer",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Are Phoenix Gravity POSTreat Fluoride Removal Filters compatible with my existing Phoenix Gravity system and filters?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes, Phoenix Gravity POSTreat Fluoride Removal Filters are designed to be fully compatible with Phoenix Gravity systems. They sit in the lower chamber of most standard gravity-fed filtration units. However, we always recommend confirming thread(nozzle) size to ensure seamless installation. If you need help determining compatibility, our team is here to assist!</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_answer_qBYUKg": {
          "type": "question_answer",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do I need one POSTreat Fluoride Removal Filter for each Carbon Filter?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes, you'll need one POSTreat Fluoride Removal Filter for each carbon Filter in your system. The<strong> </strong>POSTreat Fluoride Removal Filters are designed as a 1-to-1 companion product, meaning each fluoride removal filter connects directly to one carbon Filter.</p><p></p>"
          }
        },
